The attached image illustrates the dendrimer-like structure of phytoglycogen nanoparticles, referred to as Nano-11 in the PDF. As described, these α-D-glucan nanoparticles are highly branched and dense, with molecular density increasing from the core outwards, similar to synthetic dendrimers. This characteristic structure, originating from a genetic variant of sweet corn lacking a debranching enzyme, provides the basis for their functionalization and allows for properties like positive surface charge, enabling efficient antigen adsorption and uptake by dendritic cells, which are key to their adjuvant efficacy discussed in the research.